  "verbalization": "Golodirsen is associated with Muscular Dystrophy through a chain of indications that link it to Duchenne and Becker Muscular Dystrophy, both of which are forms of the condition. The evidence suggests that Golodirsen may act as a potential therapeutic agent for muscular dystrophy by targeting pathways involved in the disease, as indicated by its relationship with Eteplirsen, a drug also used for muscular dystrophy. The shared indication with Eteplirsen implies a possible mechanism of action that could be relevant to both drugs, potentially involving similar molecular targets or pathways. The presence of Ataluren as an intermediate in another path further highlights the complexity of the relationship, but the core evidence points to a shared therapeutic role in muscular dystrophy. The integration of these paths suggests that Golodirsen may be repurposed for muscular dystrophy, leveraging its existing indication for related conditions.",
